User → DevOps Agent (ADK-based)
What happens

A user types a question in the UI (browser / curl / chat UI).

Example:

Why did my Cloud Run service restart last night?”

Why ADK matters here

The request is not sent directly to Gemini.

It goes to the DevOps Agent, which has:

A system prompt (role, rules, behavior)

Knowledge of tools

Ability to decide what to do next

 This is the decision brain, not a simple API wrapper.

 2. DevOps Agent → Reasoning & Planning (Inside ADK)
What the agent does internally

The ADK agent:

Understands intent

Incident analysis

Root cause analysis

Log investigation

Plans actions

“I need logs”

“I need recent deployment info”

“I may need historical incidents”

This is agentic reasoning, not a single prompt.

 3. DevOps Agent → RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)
Why this step exists

LLMs do not know your environment:

Your logs

Your runbooks

Your incidents

Your Terraform / YAML

So the agent says:

“Before answering, retrieve relevant context”

What RAG does

RAG pulls real data, such as:

Cloud Logging entries

BigQuery incident tables

Runbooks from GCS

GitHub docs

Vector DB embeddings

 This makes answers grounded, accurate, and auditable.

 4. RAG ↔ External Data Sources

This is the knowledge layer.

External Data Sources include

 BigQuery

Logs

Metrics

Incident history

 GCS

SOPs

Runbooks

 Vector DB

Embedded documents

GitHub / Wikis

What happens

RAG queries these sources

Retrieves top-k relevant chunks

Sends them back to the agent as context

 5. DevOps Agent → API & DB

This path is action-oriented, not just informational.

Examples of APIs

Cloud Run API → service status

Cloud Monitoring API → CPU / memory spikes

Cloud Build API → last deployment

Kubernetes API → pod restarts

Cost APIs → billing anomalies

Databases

Incident DB

Change history DB

Configuration DB

This enables live verification, not guesswork.

 6. RAG + API Results → DevOps Agent

Now the agent has:

Retrieved knowledge (RAG)

Real-time state (APIs)

Historical context (DB)

The agent merges everything and reasons:

“Logs show OOM at 02:14, deployment at 02:10, memory limit unchanged → root cause is traffic spike”

This is multi-source reasoning, which Flask alone cannot do cleanly.

 7. DevOps Agent → Gemini (LLM via Vertex AI)
What happens here

Only after context is ready, the agent calls Gemini.

Prompt includes:

System prompt (role)

Retrieved documents

API results

User question

Gemini is used as:
 A reasoning engine
 Not a hallucination engine

8. DevOps Agent → Final Answer to User
Output includes

Clear explanation

Root cause

Evidence (logs, metrics)

Recommended action
